## 3. vCenter Identity & Security Infrastructure
The foundational internal platform daemons that handle zero-trust routing and Single Sign-On (SSO): [2, 13] 

* vmware-stsd (Security Token Service): Issues, validates, and exchanges SAML tokens to safely authenticate users or system plug-ins across vSphere.
* vmdird (VMware Directory Service): The LDAP-compliant multi-tenant directory storing configuration, multi-site domain hierarchies, user accounts, and group access maps.
* vmcad (VMware Certificate Authority): Operates a built-in Root CA mechanism that generates and dynamically provisions SSL/TLS security certificates for every host and component.
* lookupsvc (Lookup Service): A microservice directory lookup where components query and discover secure API endpoints belonging to other platform components.
* vmware-rhttpproxy / vmware-envoy: Edge gateway proxies that funnel incoming port 443 web traffic down to the targeted internal system services cleanly. [1, 2, 5, 7, 11] 

