## 4. Admin Utilities & CLI Tools
Client-side binaries and CLI structures used by system administrators to script, manage, and verify operations: [14, 15] 

* ESXCLI: A Python-based modular CLI local to the host shell used to configure storage, networking, system variables, and individual drivers.
* esxtop: A real-time, terminal-based resource performance monitor displaying extreme granular detail regarding CPU, Memory, Storage latency, and VM kernel drops.
* vSphere PowerCLI: A Windows/Linux PowerShell module packed with hundreds of cmdlets to automate bulk deployment, configuration changes, and report pulling across thousands of objects.
* VMware Tools: An internal suite of utilities installed directly inside a guest VM operating system to synchronize clock times, pass heartbeats to hostd, and run specialized VMXNET3 optimized virtual drivers.
* vmkfstools: A raw ESXi shell terminal binary used directly by storage admins to clone, raw-format, resize, or clean VMDK virtual disk blocks. [14, 15, 16, 17] 

